y path has historically lifted the basket P/E by about 1.5 points. That works out to about 0.75 turns per 25bp.\n- If the CMA is right and the market is wrong, the 19x forward P/E falls to roughly 18.25x, a drop of about 4%. If there is no cut, it falls to about 17.5x. Faster easing would add about 0.75 turns per extra 25bp.\n- n6 assumes the 19x already reflects the futures pricing, because the factsheet doesn't say.\n\n**Earnings**\n- Consensus expects 2027 EPS growth of about 14% for the holdings, and estimates have risen 3% over the past quarter (n7.r1).\n- That gives a PEG of about 1.4. This is reasonable for grid-equipment names but not cheap.\n- Growth leans on backlog conversion at Voltaris (14% of the fund) and Tarnwell (11%). A slip at either would put the 14% at risk.\n- The earnings evidence is thin. It rests on a single consensus figure with no range of estimates, and per-holding estimates and the vltx_iv and vltx_rv volatility series weren't checked.\n\n**Net**\n- 14% growth more than offsets a de-rating of about 4% under the CMA base case. Earnings growth with an unchanged multiple gives about 14% upside. A 4% de-rating on top of that still leaves roughly 9–10% price upside.\n- The case weakens if the CMA holds rates flat and conversion also slips at the top two holdings. That would mean a 1.5-turn compression and lower earnings together.","ttft_ms":5959,"type":"result","duration_ms":59974,"uuid":"f216ff68-9f76-4049-b247-5d1cdfe509e2","ttft_stream_ms":4860,"time_to_request_ms":122,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":30,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":7,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":5,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":12,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":6,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":7,"request_build":7},"tu